> How do you all decide when to zap and when not to?

Difficult to answer, that's very specific to the actual situation.

You're talking about the endgame, so I can just tell you that I
typically also carry _a lot_ wands unnecessarily around.

Offensive wands are in the late game of quite limited use to hurt
enemies. Some examples...
magic missile, force bolt - not much damage done
lightning - blinds and makes target therefore immune to Elbereth
fire - many are immune; better used to reliably engrave the E- word
death - overkill in most situations, saved for the Wizard

Where I use them is when standing on a non-permanent E- word to not
blur the engraving (as would be the case with throwing missiles) e.g.
against (master) mind flayers.

When I do not zap them?
If I would destroy (burn, shatter) something that I'd like to keep.
If I need the wands for other purpose (engraving, burning slime)
If there are more effective means (if surrounded it makes no sense
to zap at one individual, you need better solutions than fighting).
If I would kill something I'd like to have alive (pet or helpful
monster).
And I am sure a lot more situations I currently cannot think of...

